{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I wrote the above yesterday morning — at 10 o’clock I drove with Raumer and his company to St. Denis and Montmoreney. There is the famous cathedral, the burial place of the Kings of France, — it was still hung with black inside from a funeral service the previous day — in Montmoreney there is an estate, called the Hermitage, where Rousseau lived for a time?), and therefore — there are many small relics (there), also a rose bush that he planted — it is frequently visited in a pilgrim-like manner and on donkeys — (also by me with such eagerness) — . Montmoreney lies high and one ascends the higher heights behind it, — one has Paris at a distance of two hours, Montmartre and the large, rich plain dotted with villages and country houses before one. — It is beautiful around Paris, fertile, varied, — no wonder that so much life is lived in the country. This evening I am going to the Italian Opera to hear the Pesaroni — highly praised — in the morning still to the Gallery in the Louvre."}}],"created":1795080594,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":230,"prompt_tokens":334,"total_tokens":564,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-5RH3WEkfHJuqyYONdZmcfM7inCcKTmsJ","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":334,"prompt_ms":484.438,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.4504131736526946,"prompt_per_second":689.4587129828792,"predicted_n":230,"predicted_ms":5418.596,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.661991266375544,"predicted_per_second":42.26187004899424}}